# Forge — Cursor Rules

Canonical reference: **CLAUDE.md** (read first and in full).

## Quick Orientation

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| FastAPI app + all routes | `forge/api/main.py` |
| Pipecat voice pipeline | `forge/pipeline/persona_bot.py` |
| All prompts | `forge/prompts.py` — never inline LLM strings |
| Storage shim | `forge/storage.py` — never `import boto3` directly |
| RAG | `forge/rag/retriever.py` |
| Transcript scorer | `forge/ingestion/transcript_scorer.py` |
| Frontend dashboard | `forge/frontend/app/page.tsx` |

## Subsystem Docs (read when editing that module)

- `forge/api/CLAUDE.md` — route patterns, BackgroundTasks, forbidden patterns
- `forge/pipeline/CLAUDE.md` — Gemini 3.1 Flash Live pipeline rules
- `forge/ingestion/CLAUDE.md` — transcript scorer algorithm, ingestion routing
- `forge/vanguard/CLAUDE.md` — attack sessions, semaphore pattern, session contracts

## Three Rules That Matter Most

1. **All prompts in `prompts.py`** — never inline LLM call strings anywhere else
2. **All storage via `storage.py` shim** — never `import boto3; boto3.client("s3", ...)`
3. **Long-running work in `BackgroundTasks`** — never block FastAPI's async event loop

## Model Routing

| Task | Model |
|------|-------|
| Isolated edits, boilerplate (1–2 files) | Haiku |
| Feature implementation, multi-file refactors | Sonnet |
| Architecture, security review, root-cause | Opus |
